We report a rare and novel case of involuntary movement in
SPS with amphiphysin antibodies. This article highlights the
importance of therapeutic trials to con ﬁrm the diagnosis of SPS
and the understanding of the relationship between SPS and
involuntary movement. In addition, it expands the spectrum of
known clinical manifestations of SPS.
